      "id": "ipv6-rest",
      "title": "IPv6 addressing and REST API basics",
      "domain": "D5",
      "kind": "tasks",
      "level": "intermediate",
      "minutes": 12,
      "summary": "Compress IPv6 addresses, identify address types, and match REST methods and JSON data types used in network automation.",
      "scenario": "<p>You're documenting a dual-stack rollout and an automation script that talks to a controller's REST API.</p>",
      "activities": [
        {
          "type": "fill",
          "title": "Compress IPv6 addresses",
          "prompt": "Write the shortest valid form of each address (lowercase).",
          "rows": [
            {
              "label": "2001:0db8:0000:0000:0000:ff00:0042:8329",
              "answer": [
                "2001:db8::ff00:42:8329"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "fe80:0000:0000:0000:0202:b3ff:fe1e:8329",
              "answer": [
                "fe80::202:b3ff:fe1e:8329"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "2001:0db8:0001:0000:0000:0000:0000:0001",
              "answer": [
                "2001:db8:1::1"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "match",
          "title": "Identify IPv6 address types",
          "prompt": "Match each address to its type.",
          "categories": [
            "Global unicast",
            "Link-local",
            "Unique local",
            "Multicast",
            "Loopback"
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2001:db8:acad:1::10",
              "cat": 0
            },
            {
              "text": "fe80::1",
              "cat": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "fd12:3456:789a::1",
              "cat": 2
            },
            {
              "text": "ff02::1",
              "cat": 3
            },
            {
              "text": "::1",
              "cat": 4
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "match",
          "title": "REST methods and JSON",
          "prompt": "Match each item to what it does or represents.",
          "categories": [
            "Read data",
            "Create a resource",
            "Replace or update a resource",
            "Remove a resource",
            "JSON object",
            "JSON array"
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "GET",
              "cat": 0
            },
            {
              "text": "POST",
              "cat": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "PUT",
              "cat": 2
            },
            {
              "text": "DELETE",
              "cat": 3
            },
            {
              "text": "{\"hostname\": \"R1\"}",
              "cat": 4
            },
            {
              "text": "[\"Gi0/0\", \"Gi0/1\"]",
              "cat": 5
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tasks": [
        {
          "text": "Compress all three IPv6 addresses",
          "check": {
            "activity": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Identify every IPv6 address type",
          "check": {
            "activity": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Match the REST methods and JSON types",
          "check": {
            "activity": 2
          }
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Drop leading zeros in each hextet, then replace the longest run of all-zero hextets with <code>::</code> (only once).",
        "fe80::/10 is link-local, fc00::/7 (in practice fd00::/8) is unique local, ff00::/8 is multicast.",
        "CRUD maps to REST: Create = POST, Read = GET, Update = PUT/PATCH, Delete = DELETE."
      ],
      "review": "<p>IPv6 compression, address types and REST/JSON basics are all quick CCNA points once the rules are automatic.</p>"
    },
